      "message": "fix(thread): crest allowance only over a round hole wall (#1205 merge)\n\nMerging main's #1205 hole-wall law into the thread mill let the crest\nregion and the root-radius solid law excuse crests cutting 0.32 mm into\nan octagon's flats with no warning. The two thread readings now apply\nonly where every threaded hole is a tessellated circle about its axis\n(verify::hole_is_round, #1205's facet_sag and WALL_SAG); a polygonal\nhole keeps its own rim and the full tooth radius, so cutting a flat is\na gouge again. Round-hole thread goldens are unchanged.\n\nThe thread-mill golden gets its real gate verdict in solid_law_goldens\n(posted_gates/thread.rs: the real op, its blocking warnings and the\npost's verification gate) instead of an UNJUDGED entry.\n\nRefs #894\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
