      "message": "Merge upstream/main into issue/894-thread-mill (27 files; #1071 thread laws reconciled)\n\nBoth sides kept (lists, kinds, tests, Tool fields):\nassets/tools/catalog.json, app operation/mod.rs, project/file.rs,\ntests golden_cl.rs, mcp.rs, mill2d_b.rs, operations.rs,\nposted_gates/mod.rs, solid_law_goldens.rs, tool_law.rs,\nmotion drilling/tests.rs, tests/center_cut_owed.rs, sim verify/mod.rs,\ntools catalog_asset.rs, catalog_asset_tests.rs, lib.rs, tools.rs,\nui browser_tree.rs, icons.rs, mod.rs, pages.rs, tool_icons.rs, state.rs.\nThis branch's thread-mill tool kept in hole_wall_flats.rs and mill2d_c.rs\n(main still built a Tap there).\n\nJudgements (docs/decisions/894-thread-mill.md, \"The refresh against main\"):\n- generate.rs, region law: main's thread_rims::major_rims (#1071) replaces\n  this branch's crest_region - it grows the major circle from the model's\n  own rim, never wider - and stays behind this branch's walls_round gate\n  (#894 x #1205).\n- generate.rs, solid law: main's thread grant (verify::thread_bore, full\n  cutter) replaces this branch's root_cutter, which credited the thread\n  depth against every facet. Not stacked. crest_region, root_cutter and\n  their unit tests are removed.\n- thread_op::bores: the grant reads the thread's own pitch (a single-form\n  mill's tool.pitch is only its coarsest; main passed tool.pitch) and is\n  empty over a wall that is not round.\n- The crossing stand-down for Thread stays: with it off, this branch's\n  rides still convict under main's touching-chords law.\n- stamp.rs: main's split taken; the thread mills' digest clause moved to\n  stamp_tool.rs. Kind numbers: Electrode keeps 13, thread mills 14 and 15\n  (stamp digest, tool page list, state.rs).\n- Main's thread_mill_rim.rs and coarse_rims.rs now mount a thread mill and\n  state pitch/hand (a Tap on a Thread op is refused by this branch's tool\n  law); no assertion changed. electrode.rs and thread_mill.rs Tool\n  literals take the other side's new fields.\n\nNo golden moved, no snapshot PNG, no process file.\n\nRefs #894\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
